["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>In late October, legal light ends about an hour after sunset, when it is already dark. Almost every deer hunt ends with a walk out at night. Plan it like a second hunt.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"At night the hunter walks a short leg to a creek, follows the creek as a handrail, and reaches the road, which is the catching feature. Longer than a straight line, but hard to get lost.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1f2a3a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Night route: big, simple, short legs</text><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"60\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Road: catching feature</text><path d=\"M300 290 C 280 230, 320 180, 300 120 C 290 100, 250 80, 220 72\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"215\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#9ec5ea\" text-anchor=\"start\">Creek: handrail</text><path d=\"M80 280 C 140 250, 230 260, 290 250\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"280\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffb38a\" text-anchor=\"start\">You</text><path d=\"M290 250 C 280 200, 300 150, 280 110 C 270 90, 240 80, 225 76\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"110\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Night: walk to the creek,</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"128\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">follow it to the road.</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"146\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Longer, but you cannot</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"164\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">get lost.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Night routes are big and simple: handrail to catching feature (Tip).</li><li>Prepare in daylight: waypoint, back bearing, lamp.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this lesson adds</summary><ul><li>Light times and turnaround: <a href=\"#/s/route-planning/0\">Planning a route</a>. Compass tricks: <a href=\"#/s/compass-mastery/0\">Compass mastery</a>. Phone and battery: <a href=\"#/s/gps-phone-battery/0\">GPS, phone and battery</a>.</li><li>This lesson: night eyes, lights and the law, the before dark routine, walking out, finding north by the stars, and what to do when unsure.</li><li>Mid October at Heffley Creek: sunset about 18:08, legal light ends about 19:08, civil twilight ends about 18:41 (85%, my calculation).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Do</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Waypoint the truck in daylight</td><td>The phone leads you back</td></tr><tr><td>Write the back bearing on your hand</td><td>Works when the phone dies</td></tr><tr><td>Pick a catching feature</td><td>The road you cannot miss</td></tr><tr><td>Unload at legal light end</td><td>No hunting after hours, no hunting with a light</td></tr><tr><td>Red light, low</td><td>Keeps your night eyes</td></tr><tr><td>Short legs on handrails</td><td>Hard to get lost</td></tr><tr><td>Stop when unsure</td><td>Night mistakes grow fast</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the key points in full</summary><ol><li>Big game and upland bird hunting ends 1 hour after sunset (99%, synopsis page 11, see the Rule Book).</li><li>It is unlawful to hunt with the aid of a light <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. A headlamp to walk in or out is not hunting with a light (90%, Rule Book, my reading).</li><li>Following a wounded animal with a firearm after hours, or with a headlamp, is hunting outside hours and with a light (85%, Rule Book reading in <a href=\"#/s/blood-trailing/0\">Blood trailing</a>).</li><li>Night vision takes 20 to 40 minutes to build and a few seconds of bright light breaks it down (90%, US National Park Service).</li><li>Dim deep red light preserves night vision (90%, same).</li><li>In the dark, use handrails and catching features, not long straight bearings (Tip, from orienteering).</li><li>Lost: stop, stay put, shelter, call (75%, AdventureSmart).</li></ol></details><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A curve of night vision rising over 30 minutes in the dark, most of it by 20 to 30 minutes. A bright white light drops it back to zero in seconds.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Eyes need 20 to 30 min in the dark</text><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M50 240 C 90 200, 110 190, 140 185 C 180 180, 200 120, 250 90 C 290 72, 330 68, 370 66\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"272\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"272\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"272\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20</text><text x=\"350\" y=\"272\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30 min</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"80\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Night</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"96\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">vision</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"266.4\" y2=\"102.3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"262.0,96.0 263.4,108.5 273.3,101.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"170\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">White light: back</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"188\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">to zero in seconds</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>20 to 40 minutes to see well in the dark <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>A few seconds of bright light resets it <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: night eyes in full</summary><ul><li>Rods in the eye use a pigment, rhodopsin, that builds up in low light. It starts after about 20 minutes and full benefit takes 20 to 40 minutes (90%, NPS, dark adaptation article).</li><li>\"A few seconds of bright light\" breaks it down and the rods stop working until it rebuilds <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Older aviation guidance gives 20 to 30 minutes for useful dark adaptation <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Tip: on a clear night with snow or a moon you may not need a lamp on an open road. In timber you will.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"At night, one hunter shines a bright white headlamp far ahead, which wipes out night vision. The other uses a dim red light pointed at the feet, which keeps it. Tip: red and low for map reading and walking near others.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1f2a3a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(100 200) scale(1.1)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#d0d6dc\"/><path d=\"M0 -23 V2 M0 2 L-7 18 M0 2 L7 18 M0 -16 L-9 -4 M0 -16 L9 -4\" stroke=\"#d0d6dc\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/></g><path d=\"M110 168 L200 230 L200 280 L110 180 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"60\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">White</text><g transform=\"translate(290 200) scale(1.1)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#d0d6dc\"/><path d=\"M0 -23 V2 M0 2 L-7 18 M0 2 L7 18 M0 -16 L-9 -4 M0 -16 L9 -4\" stroke=\"#d0d6dc\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/></g><path d=\"M300 168 L340 270 L300 275 Z\" fill=\"#e03131\" opacity=\".55\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"60\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#ff8787\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Red, low</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"95\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Far, bright</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"113\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">kills night eyes</text><text x=\"225\" y=\"95\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ff8787\" text-anchor=\"start\">At your feet,</text><text x=\"225\" y=\"113\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ff8787\" text-anchor=\"start\">keeps night eyes</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>White for walking hard ground. Red, low, for maps and near your brother (Tip).</li><li>Never shine a light in another hunter's eyes (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: lights in full</summary><ul><li>Deep red light does not break down rhodopsin. Bright red still can, so dim red is best (90%, NPS).</li><li>Red light makes red ink on a map hard to see (65%, older aviation handbook).</li><li>Headlamp habits (Tip): beam on the trail at your feet, not at the horizon; turn your head, not your whole body; warn before you switch to bright.</li><li>Animals react to a moving light as pure motion (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/deer-mind/0\">Deer senses and mind</a>.</li><li>Two lights each, plus spare lithium cells (Tip). Energizer lists its lithium AA from minus 40 to 60°C <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: at night a hunter swings a bright white headlamp beam across the timber. The beam sweeps over a deer, which bolts. Tip: a moving light is pure motion to animals; keep it low and steady.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1f2a3a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">A swinging beam is pure motion</text><g fill=\"#33415a\"><polygon points=\"60,209.6 42.0,260 78.0,260\"/><rect x=\"56.4\" y=\"260\" width=\"7.2\" height=\"10.8\"/></g><g fill=\"#33415a\"><polygon points=\"120,209.6 102.0,260 138.0,260\"/><rect x=\"116.4\" y=\"260\" width=\"7.2\" height=\"10.8\"/></g><g fill=\"#33415a\"><polygon points=\"330,209.6 312.0,260 348.0,260\"/><rect x=\"326.4\" y=\"260\" width=\"7.2\" height=\"10.8\"/></g><g fill=\"#33415a\"><polygon points=\"360,209.6 342.0,260 378.0,260\"/><rect x=\"356.4\" y=\"260\" width=\"7.2\" height=\"10.8\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(250 230) scale(0.9 0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"20\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#7a5a3a\"/><path d=\"M14 -5 L22 -18 L28 -17 L24 -6 Z\" fill=\"#7a5a3a\"/><circle cx=\"25\" cy=\"-19\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#7a5a3a\"/><path d=\"M-12 6 v14 M-6 6 v14 M10 6 v14 M15 6 v14\" stroke=\"#7a5a3a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(110 250) scale(0.9)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#d0d6dc\"/><path d=\"M0 -23 V2 M0 2 L-7 18 M0 2 L7 18 M0 -16 L-9 -4 M0 -16 L9 -4\" stroke=\"#d0d6dc\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g><path d=\"M118 220 L380 160 L380 240 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff\" opacity=\".35\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"-12 118 220;10 118 220;-12 118 220\" dur=\"3s\" repeatCount=\"2\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"280\" y=\"140\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ff8787\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Deer: gone</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>A moving beam across a slope moves deer. Keep it low and steady. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Walking in before light? Point the lamp at your boots (Tip).</li><li>Using a light to find or hold game is illegal <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: lights and the law</summary><ul><li>\"To hunt wildlife by the use of, or with the aid of a light or illuminating device\" is unlawful (99%, synopsis page 11, item 38, as quoted in the Rule Book).</li><li>That covers a spotlight, headlamp, weapon light or truck lights used to find, hold or shoot game (95%, Rule Book, my reading).</li><li>Rule Book: <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Legal methods</a> and <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts/0\">Unlawful acts</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"5\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Five things before the light goes</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 5</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Drop a waypoint at the truck before you leave it.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Waypoint the truck</text><g transform=\"translate(200 170)\"><rect x=\"-22\" y=\"-14\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M8 -14 h10 l6 7 v7 h-16 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"2\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"2\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"120\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"125\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">Truck waypoint</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Before you leave it</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Waypoint the truck before you leave it.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Write the back bearing to the truck or road on your hand.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Note the back bearing</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"80\" width=\"140\" height=\"120\" rx=\"40\" fill=\"#f4d9c4\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Back 220°</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Write it on your hand</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Write the back bearing on your hand.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pick the road as a catching feature you cannot miss.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pick a catching feature</text><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"80\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Road</text><g transform=\"translate(200 240) scale(0.8)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M0 -23 V2 M0 2 L-7 18 M0 2 L7 18 M0 -16 L-9 -4 M0 -16 L9 -4\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/></g><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"172.0\" y2=\"107.4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/><polygon points=\"170.0,100.0 167.1,112.2 178.7,109.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">The road behind everything</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Pick the catching feature: the road.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Check the headlamp, spare lithium cells and a second light at the truck.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lamp check at the truck</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"110\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"135\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#f2c70c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"130\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">+ spares</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"150\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">+ 2nd light</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lamp, spare cells, backup light</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Check the lamp, spare cells, second light.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"At the end of legal light, unload and walk out together.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Unload at legal light end</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"120\" width=\"240\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#555555\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"190\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Chamber and magazine empty</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Then walk out together</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>5.</b> Legal light ends: unload, walk out together.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Do steps 1 to 4 at the truck, every time (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the routine in full</summary><ul><li>Truck waypoint: Tools, Waypoint, At my location, icon Parking (99%, Hunt Map).</li><li>Start Go &amp; Track at the truck if the route is new. Back to start gives distance and heading the whole way <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Battery plan: <a href=\"#/s/gps-phone-battery/0\">GPS, phone and battery</a>.</li><li>Write the bearing from your hunting spot back to the road or truck on the back of your hand (Tip).</li><li>Unload at legal light end: chamber and magazine empty before walking out, and empty before the firearm goes in or on the vehicle (99% for the vehicle rule, Rule Book item 28; walking out unloaded is Tip).</li><li>Walk out together. Agree a meet point if you are split up (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"At night the hunter walks a short leg to a creek, follows the creek as a handrail, and reaches the road, which is the catching feature. Longer than a straight line, but hard to get lost.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1f2a3a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Night route: big, simple, short legs</text><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"60\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Road: catching feature</text><path d=\"M300 290 C 280 230, 320 180, 300 120 C 290 100, 250 80, 220 72\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"215\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#9ec5ea\" text-anchor=\"start\">Creek: handrail</text><path d=\"M80 280 C 140 250, 230 260, 290 250\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"280\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffb38a\" text-anchor=\"start\">You</text><path d=\"M290 250 C 280 200, 300 150, 280 110 C 270 90, 240 80, 225 76\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"110\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Night: walk to the creek,</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"128\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">follow it to the road.</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"146\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Longer, but you cannot</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"164\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">get lost.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Walk to a handrail, follow it to the catching feature (Tip).</li><li>Longer is fine. Lost is not.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: walking out in full</summary><ul><li>In the dark, prefer a creek, a road, a fence, a cutblock edge or a ridge over a long straight bearing (Tip, orienteering handrails).</li><li>Shorter legs: check the compass and the phone more often (Tip).</li><li>Count paces on legs where you have no handrail (75%, see Compass mastery).</li><li>Aim off when heading for the road so you know which way to turn <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Slow down on steep ground: red slopes in Slope steepness are 30 to 45 degrees (99%, Hunt Map). Check it before dark.</li><li>Stay away from cliff edges (touching contours) and creek banks in the dark (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The Go and Track screen while recording shows Back to start: 1.9 kilometres, heading 214 degrees, south west, and GPS good. Walk that heading with the compass.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"30\" width=\"180\" height=\"250\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><rect x=\"120\" y=\"44\" width=\"160\" height=\"222\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"72\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Recording</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"104\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">2.8 km</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"104\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">2:41</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"120\" width=\"144\" height=\"90\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8f2e0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"136\" y=\"142\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Back to start:</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"162\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">1.9 km,</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"182\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">heading 214°</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"200\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">(SW)</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"240\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" text-anchor=\"start\">GPS good (6 m)</text><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"286.3\" y2=\"169.4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"280.0,165.0 285.5,176.3 292.5,166.4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"225\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Walk this</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"243\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">heading</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Go &amp; Track: Back to start gives distance and heading <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Walk that heading with the compass, phone back in the warm pocket (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: back to start in full</summary><ul><li>Back to start shows something like \"1.9 km, heading 214° (SW)\". The green dot marks the start (99%, Hunt Map).</li><li>Waypoint only, no track? Open the truck waypoint and use Measure from your location to read distance and bearing (Tip; Measure shows the bearing of the last leg, 99%).</li><li>A heading on the phone is from true north. Your compass set to 15 east also reads true <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Weak GPS under timber? Wait for \"GPS good\" before you trust it (99% app wording; Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The Big Dipper in the night sky. A dashed line runs from its two end stars, the pointers, up to Polaris, the North Star, about five times the gap between them. Polaris marks north.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1f2a3a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Find north by the stars</text><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"250\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"240\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"232\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"222\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"255\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"262\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"215\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M60 250 L100 240 L135 232 L165 222 L230 215 L225 262 L170 255 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9aa5b1\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"230\" y1=\"212\" x2=\"252.9\" y2=\"52.6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><polygon points=\"254.0,45.0 246.4,55.0 258.4,56.7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"255\" cy=\"38\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"272\" y=\"44\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffd8a8\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Polaris: north</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"245\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffd8a8\" text-anchor=\"start\">pointers</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"265\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Big Dipper: the two end stars point</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"283\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">up to Polaris, about 5 times their gap.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Line from Merak through Dubhe, about 5 times the gap: Polaris <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Polaris sits about 51° up at Heffley Creek, due north <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: stars in full</summary><ul><li>\"Draw a line from Merak through Dubhe, and go about five times the Merak/Dubhe distance to Polaris.\" (90%, EarthSky)</li><li>Polaris climbs higher as you go north, overhead at the pole, on the horizon at the equator (90%, EarthSky). Its height in degrees is about your latitude: about 51 degrees at Heffley Creek, 49 at Mission (85%, standard astronomy).</li><li>Polaris marks true north, within about 1 degree <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>A backup only. Clouds are common in October (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Flowchart for night: 1 stop and turn the lamp off for a minute. 2 phone Back to start heading. 3 compass to the handrail. 4 still lost: stay put, shelter and call. Do not just walk downhill in the dark.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"30\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Not sure where you are at night?</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"45\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"67\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 STOP. Lamp off a minute.</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"88.3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,96.0 206.1,85.0 193.9,85.0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"98\" width=\"260\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"120\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2 Phone: Back to start heading</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"133\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"141.3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,149.0 206.1,138.0 193.9,138.0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"151\" width=\"260\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"173\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 Compass to the handrail</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"186\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"194.3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,202.0 206.1,191.0 193.9,191.0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"204\" width=\"300\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"226\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4 Still lost? Stay. Shelter, call.</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Do not walk downhill in the dark to get out.</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"288\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Draws end in cliffs and creeks (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>STOP. Lamp off a minute. Think.</li><li>Lost for real: stay put and call. Do not walk down blind draws (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: lost at night in full</summary><ul><li>STOP: Stop, Think, Observe, Plan (90%, Bush safety).</li><li>\"If you become lost or disoriented, the best thing you can do is stay put.\" (75%, AdventureSmart guidance via search and rescue page)</li><li>Shelter from wind, insulate from the ground, fire only if safe and allowed (Tip; check fire bans, see <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety/0\">Bush safety</a>).</li><li>Satellite SOS or messenger: open sky, clear horizon (95%, Apple). See <a href=\"#/s/gps-phone-battery/0\">GPS, phone and battery</a>.</li><li>Your trip plan's call time brings help to the right place <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Tip: walking downhill in the dark to \"get out\" often ends at a cliff or creek in a steep draw.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2eVVkHfqh0U\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Hug-A-Tree &amp; Survive film</b><small>Hug a tree: stay put when lost.<br>AdventureSmart, YouTube, 12 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of how long to wait before following a hit deer: heart or lungs 30 minutes, muscle or leg 30 to 60 minutes, liver 4 to 6 hours, gut 6 to 8 hours or overnight, not sure several hours.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">How long to wait before you follow</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">0 h</text><line x1=\"206\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"206\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">2 h</text><line x1=\"262\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"262\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">4 h</text><line x1=\"318\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">6 h</text><line x1=\"374\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"374\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"374\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">8 h</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Heart or lungs</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"52\" width=\"14.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2e7d32\"/><text x=\"170.0\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">30 min</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Muscle or leg</text><rect x=\"164.0\" y=\"90\" width=\"14.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2e7d32\"/><text x=\"184\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">30 to 60 min</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Liver</text><rect x=\"262\" y=\"128\" width=\"56\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"256\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">4 to 6 h</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Gut</text><rect x=\"318\" y=\"166\" width=\"56\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/><text x=\"312\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">6 to 8 h, or overnight</text><line x1=\"374\" y1=\"179\" x2=\"396.0\" y2=\"179.0\" stroke=\"#b3261e\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M389.7 182.0 L396.0 179.0 L389.7 176.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b3261e\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"144\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Not sure</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">several hours. Back out.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Rain coming? Go sooner (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mark the spot, the line and the time. Then follow the rules for after hours (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: late shots in full</summary><ul><li>Mark where you stood, where the animal was, and the direction it went with waypoints (Tip).</li><li>After legal light, trailing with a firearm or a light is hunting after hours and with a light (85%, Rule Book reading). See <a href=\"#/s/blood-trailing/0\">Blood trailing</a> for what you can do and who to call.</li><li>Tip: a late evening shot means a night walk with meat. Pack the headlamp, rope and game bags every time.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Headlamp with red mode</td><td>Hands free, night eyes</td></tr><tr><td>Second small light</td><td>Lamps fail</td></tr><tr><td>Spare lithium cells</td><td>Cold proof <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Compass, bearing on hand</td><td>Phone backup</td></tr><tr><td>Phone, power bank</td><td>Track and Back to start</td></tr><tr><td>Warm layer, toque</td><td>Night temperatures drop fast</td></tr><tr><td>Whistle</td><td>Three blasts for help (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: gear notes</summary><ul><li>Prices: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> at a local store. See <a href=\"#/s/pack-kit/0\">Day pack and car kit</a> for the full kit list.</li><li>Practise changing headlamp cells in the dark with gloves on (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Write the back bearing to the truck or road on your hand.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"26\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Note the back bearing</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"80\" width=\"140\" height=\"120\" rx=\"40\" fill=\"#f4d9c4\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Back 220°</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Write it on your hand</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Learn the walk out in daylight. The dark only lets you use what you already know.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>No truck waypoint and no back bearing.</li><li>Blasting a white lamp at your brother's eyes, then at the hillside.</li><li>Cutting straight down a dark draw to \"save time\".</li></ul></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the mistakes in full</summary><ul><li>No truck waypoint and no back bearing. The phone dies at 18:50 and nothing else knows the way.</li><li>Blasting a bright white lamp around: your night eyes are gone, and every animal on the slope sees it.</li><li>Cutting straight down a dark draw instead of walking the road. Draws end in creeks, cliffs and blowdown.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Pick a 1 km walk you know. Walk it at last light with only a red lamp and your compass. Your brother walks behind with the phone and says nothing unless you leave the route.</p></aside><div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"fn-night-out\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-night-out:0\"><span>Truck waypoint saved</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-night-out:1\"><span>Back bearing written on hand</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-night-out:2\"><span>Catching feature named out loud</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-night-out:3\"><span>Headlamp, second light, spare cells</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-night-out:4\"><span>Unloaded at legal light end</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"fn-night-out:5\"><span>Walked out together</span></label></div>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Waypoint, bearing, road</td><td>The three before dark</td></tr><tr><td>Red and low, slow you go</td><td>Light habits</td></tr><tr><td>Twenty to forty</td><td>Minutes to night eyes</td></tr><tr><td>Five times the pointers</td><td>Polaris from the Big Dipper</td></tr><tr><td>Hour after sunset, rifle unset</td><td>Unload at legal light end</td></tr><tr><td>Downhill blind is cliff and brook</td><td>Do not chase draws in the dark</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Big, simple, short:</strong> night route legs.</li><li><strong>STOP:</strong> Stop, Think, Observe, Plan.</li><li><strong>Three of anything:</strong> three whistle blasts or three flashes mean help (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.nps.gov/articles/dark-adaptation-of-the-human-eye-and-the-value-of-red-flashlights.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">US National Park Service: dark adaptation of the human eye and the value of red flashlights</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://earthsky.org/brightest-stars/polaris-the-present-day-north-star/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EarthSky: Polaris, the present day North Star</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, page 11 (hours, lights), as quoted in the Rule Book <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Legal methods</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Sunset and twilight times: my calculation, Heffley Creek, Pacific time <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>AdventureSmart stay put guidance, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://data.energizer.com/pdfs/liaa_sellsheet_may2010.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Energizer lithium AA sell sheet</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul>","<ul><li>Hunt Map Go &amp; Track and Back to start: app code, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Night routines and route choice: hunter and orienteering experience, labelled Tip.</li></ul>"]